<title>UK: CSCE July sugar delivery totals 57,800 tons -trade.</title>
<headline>CSCE July sugar delivery totals 57,800 tons -trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total of 1,156 lots of raw sugar, equivalent to 57,800 long tons, was delivered against the New York Coffee, Sugar and Cocoa Exchange's (CSCE) July contract, European trade sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The contract expired at close of business on Monday. The CSCE has yet to confirm the deliveries.</p>
<p>The trade sources gave the following details:</p>
<p>Deliverer	Lots     Receivers		  Port</p>
<p>Pru-Bache	 312     Man		   Paranagua</p>
<p>Pru-Bache	  29     Man		   Guatemala</p>
<p>Merril Lynch    236     Man		   Paranagua</p>
<p>Cargill	   394     Man		   Santos</p>
<p>Dreyfus	   185     Man		   Santos</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
